  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R^2$ be a function given by $f(x)=(x^m,x^n)$, where $x\\in\\mathbb R$ and $m,n$ are fixed positive integers. Suppose that $f$ is one-one. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "both $m$ and $n$ must be odd;",
    "B": "at least one of $m$ and $n$ must be odd;",
    "C": "exactly one of $m$ and $n$ must be odd;",
    "D": "neither $m$ nor $n$ can be odd."
  },
  "answer": "B",
